VIM EDITOR COMMANDS CHEAT SHEET
===============================

1. UNDO AND REDO
----------------
u                   : Undo the last change
Ctrl + r            : Redo a change that was undone

2. SEARCH AND REPLACE
---------------------
:%s/pat/rep/g       : Replace "pat" with "rep" in ALL lines and ALL occurrences
:%s/pat/rep/        : Replace "pat" with "rep" in ALL lines (first occurrence only)
?pattern            : Search backwards for "pattern"
f{char}             : Search for {char} forward along the single/current line
cw                  : Change word (delete word and enter Insert mode)
r{char}             : Replace the single character under cursor with {char}

3. SORTING AND FILTERING
------------------------
:sort!              : Sort lines in descending order
:sort               : Sort lines in ascending order
!{motion}{command}  : Filter text through an external command (e.g., !Gsort)

4. NAVIGATION AND MOVEMENT
--------------------------
:set nu             : Set/Display line numbers
:6                  : Move cursor to line number 6
6G                  : Alternate command to move to line number 6
$                   : Move to the end of the current line
w                   : Move forward one word
b                   : Move backward one word
e                   : Move to the end of the current word
[[                  : Move backward to previous section
]]                  : Move forward to next section
gd                  : Jump to local variable definition
Ctrl + g            : Check current file status (name, line count, position)
m{a-z}              : Mark current position (e.g., ma). Jump back with 'a

5. COPY, PASTE, AND EDITING
---------------------------
yy                  : Copy (yank) current line
p                   : Paste after cursor
P                   : Paste before cursor
3yy                 : Copy 3 lines (starting from cursor)
5p                  : Paste the copied text 5 times
J                   : Join current line with the line below (joins words across lines)
Ctrl + k {c1}{c2}   : Insert digraph (Insert Mode only). E.g., Ctrl+k OK = ✓

6. MACROS (RECORDING)
---------------------
q{a-z}              : Start recording macro into register a-z
q                   : Stop recording
@{a-z}              : Execute/Display the macro stored in register a-z
